@segment 35-36 Shimmering Flats & Dustwallow Marsh
@start-level 35
# Added 2026-11-11 from the Questie audit (tools/questie_near.py): 1204 Mudrock Soup and Bugs (2850 XP; about 30 turtle kills on the north-east coast, on the loop).
# Skyborne Mage segment (the Skyborne Druid route's segment 14 with the class parts replaced; same quests, order, binds and flight points).
# Carried in (segment 13's carry-out): 1179 The Brassbolts Brothers (Wizzle, Mirage Raceway), 1264 The Missing Diplomat (Commander Samaul,
# Theramore), 1947 Journey to the Marsh (mage class quest, from Jennea Cannon in Stormwind at 30; handed in at Tabetha here).
# 525 (Southshore), 563 (Stormwind), 1457 and 1467 (Ironforge) ride along until the Eastern Kingdoms.
@carry 525,563,1179,1264,1302,1457,1467,1947,98463
# Prerequisites of the carried quests, handed in by earlier segments: 514 -> 525, 562 -> 563, 1250 -> 1264, 1456 -> 1457, 1466 -> 1467.
@done 514,562,1250,1456,1466
# The long walk of the route: Astranaar -> Ratchet -> Great Lift -> Shimmering Flats -> Gadgetzan -> back to the Dustwallow road.
# It collects the Ratchet, Gadgetzan and Theramore flight points for the later Kalimdor trips. No training in this segment:
# the next one trains in Stormwind (the Hearthstone is needed for the Theramore loop, and a Teleport: Stormwind from Kalimdor
# would leave no way back).
# Hearth: Nijel's Point at the start (useless here), Theramore from the first Theramore stop on.
# Carry-out (8): 1106 Martek the Exiled (Badlands), 1111 Wharfmaster Dizzywig and 1178 Goblin Sponsorship (Ratchet, next Kalimdor trip),
# 5762 Hemet Nesingwary (Stranglethorn), plus 525, 563, 1457, 1467.
# Left out on purpose: 1135 Highperch Venom, 1203 Jarl Needs a Blade (needs a crafted sword), 1282 (280 XP), the Thalanaar quests.
# Deviations from the druid source:
# - All hints rewritten for a mage (the long walks are plain walks; poison cannot be cured; Polymorph / Frost Nova fights).
# - Mage class quest: 1947 is handed in at Tabetha's hut (Dustwallow Marsh 46.1, 57.1), a short walk east of Balos Jacken at
#   Lost Point, just before the hearth to Theramore. Her two quests are NOT taken (an N step says why): 1949 Hidden Secrets goes
#   to the Mirage Raceway, which this segment has already left, and its chain (1950 -> 1951 Rituals of Power) needs a book from
#   the Scarlet Monastery; 1948 Items of Power wants a Jade and comes back to Tabetha, where the route does not return; the
#   wand quest 1952 needs 1951. (The Horde mage route did 1949 and 1950 because it reached the raceway AFTER Tabetha.)
# - The end: Teleport: Ironforge from Theramore replaces the boat to Menethil Harbor and the Menethil -> Ironforge flight that
#   opened segment 15 (no quest or new flight point on that leg; the boat stays as the fallback in the step text).

# ---------- Nijel's Point -> Astranaar -> Ratchet ----------
N Have 3 Soothing Spices in your bags | You bought them in Southshore earlier. None left? No problem: Helenia Olden sells them in Theramore (66.4, 51.5), you then do Jarl's two quests on the loop out of Theramore later in this segment.
FLY Astranaar @ Desolace, 64.7, 10.5 | Baritanas Skyriver, the hippogryph master at Nijel's Point
N Walk from Astranaar to Ratchet @ The Barrens, 63.1, 37.2 | A long walk, there is no faster way yet. Take the road east from Astranaar, then the road south into the Barrens. The border gate (Mor'shan Rampart) is a Horde guard post: do not stop, run straight through or around the side. In the Barrens stay on the road south, leave it before the Crossroads (a Horde town, pass it well to the east) and follow the road east to Ratchet on the coast. Ratchet is neutral. This is Classic geography, not re-checked.
F Ratchet @ The Barrens, 63.1, 37.2 | Bragok, the flight master near the dock

# ---------- Down to the Shimmering Flats ----------
N Walk south to the Great Lift and on to the Mirage Raceway @ Thousand Needles, 78.0, 77.0 | Another long walk. From Ratchet go back west to the main road and follow it south through the whole Barrens (pass Camp Taurajo, a Horde camp, at a distance) to the Great Lift at the south end. Ride the lift down into Thousand Needles and follow the canyon road east, past Freewind Post (Horde, up on a mesa: just keep walking), until the canyon opens into the white salt flats. The Mirage Raceway is in the middle of the flats.
T 1179 | Wizzle Brassbolts, on the gnome side of the raceway
A 1105 | Wizzle Brassbolts
A 1104 | Fizzle Brassbolts, next to him
A 1106 | Fizzle Brassbolts. A letter for Martek in the Badlands: keep it, a later segment hands it in.
A 1110 | Kravel Koalbeard, a few steps away
A 5762 | Kravel Koalbeard. A crate for Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn: keep it for the next segment.
A 1111 | Kravel Koalbeard. An order for Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet: keep it for the next Kalimdor trip.
A 1176 | Pozzik, on the goblin side of the track
A 1175 | Trackmaster Zherin, at the east end of the goblin side
C 1105,1104,1175:1 @ Thousand Needles, 76.0, 60.0 | North half of the flats. Sparkleshell Tortoises (30-31) and Snappers (34-35) drop the shells, Scorpid Reavers (31-32) the venom, and the Saltstone Basilisks (30-31) only live up here: kill 10. Salt Flats Scavengers (the vultures here) drop Hollow Vulture Bones, Saltstone Crystalhides count for Zherin, and every Rocket Car Rubble pile on the ground holds car parts: pick up all you pass. Everything here is below your level: Frostbolt and Fire Blast one at a time, drink conjured water when your mana runs low.
C 1175,1176,1110 @ Thousand Needles, 78.0, 85.0 | South half, below the raceway. Saltstone Gazers (34-35) are only down here: kill 6. Finish the 10 Crystalhides, get the rest of the 10 vulture bones from the Salt Flats Vultures and keep picking up rubble until you have 30 Rocket Car Parts. Scorpid Terrors and Sparkleshell Borers here also drop venom and shells if you are short.
T 1105 | Wizzle Brassbolts
T 1104 | Fizzle Brassbolts
T 1110 | Kravel Koalbeard
T 1176 | Pozzik
A 1178 | Pozzik. A message for Gazlowe in Ratchet: keep it for the next Kalimdor trip.
T 1175 | Trackmaster Zherin

# ---------- Gadgetzan flight point ----------
N Walk south into Tanaris to Gadgetzan @ Tanaris, 51.0, 29.3 | Leave the flats by the pass in the south wall and follow the road south to the goblin town. The desert animals near the road are level 40 and up: stay on the road and keep moving.
F Gadgetzan @ Tanaris, 51.0, 29.3 | Bera Stonehammer, the Alliance gryphon master on the north side of town. Nothing else to do here yet.

# ---------- Back north and into Dustwallow Marsh ----------
N Walk back north to the Dustwallow road @ Dustwallow Marsh, 29.7, 47.6 | Back through the flats and the canyon, up the Great Lift and north on the Barrens road. A side road branches off east into Dustwallow Marsh a little north of the lift. The first thing on it is the burnt-out Shady Rest Inn. The marsh animals are 35-38: pull one at a time with Frostbolt, Frost Nova and step back when they reach you. You cannot cure the spider poison: bandage or eat after the fight.
A 1284 | The Suspicious Hoofprint, a mark on the ground in front of the inn ruins
A 1253 | The Black Shield, hanging over the fireplace of the ruins
A 1252 | The Theramore Guard Badge, lying on the floor boards of the ruins
A 1177 | Mudcrush Durtfeet, an ogre standing by the road north-east of the inn, just south of Brackenwall Village. Brackenwall is a Horde ogre town: do not go further north than him. If he is hostile to you or you cannot reach him, skip his quest (this step, the murloc step and the hand-in).
A 1218 | "Swamp Eye" Jarl at the Swamplight Manor, the lonely house in the north of the marsh. Follow the road east and turn north.
T 1218 | "Swamp Eye" Jarl. Hand him the 3 Soothing Spices. (No spices: skip this and the next step and come back on the loop out of Theramore.)
A 1206 | "Swamp Eye" Jarl
A 1219 | The Loose Dirt mound behind Jarl's house. It gives you the Spy's Report.
C 1177 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 56.8, 15.6 | Mirefin murlocs (35-38) on the north coast, straight north of Jarl's house, and on the small islands further north-east. About one in three drops a head; you need 8. They come in twos and threes and run when low: Polymorph the second one before you start, Fire Blast or Frost Nova on runners, and if a third joins Frost Nova all of them, step back and finish them one by one.
A 1222 | "Stinky" Ignatz, standing in the swamp west of the murloc beach
C 1222 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 46.9, 17.5 | Escort: walk beside Stinky while he looks for his bogbean plant and kill whatever attacks him (swamp animals, 35-38). You cannot heal him: stay close, kill each attacker fast, Frost Nova what is on him and Polymorph a second animal. When he thanks you the quest is complete; the hand-in is in Theramore. If he dies, abandon the quest and take it again from him.
C 1206 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 32.8, 22.2 | Darkmist Cavern, in the north-west corner of the marsh. Darkmist Spiders (35-36), Recluses (36-37) and Silkspinners (38-39) all drop the eyes; you need 20. Work inwards from the entrance, one spider at a time: Frostbolt, Frost Nova when it reaches you, step back and finish it. You cannot cure the poison, so bandage or eat between pulls when it has stacked. Leave the rare Darkmist Widow (40) alone.
T 1177 | Mudcrush Durtfeet, south of the cavern
T 1206 | "Swamp Eye" Jarl. Do not take Jarl Needs a Blade: it wants a crafted sword.

# ---------- Theramore ----------
F Theramore @ Dustwallow Marsh, 67.5, 51.3 | Follow the road south-east and across the long bridge to Theramore Isle. Baldruc, the gryphon master, is in the south-east of town.
S Theramore @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.6, 45.2 | Innkeeper Janene, in the inn at the north end of town
T 1222 | Morgan Stern, in the same inn
A 1204 | Morgan Stern: Mudrock Soup and Bugs (needs level 33). The turtles are on the coast north of Theramore: you pass it on the loop below
T 1219 | A Theramore Lieutenant: the officers standing at the town gates
A 1220 | The same Theramore Lieutenant
T 1220 | Captain Garran Vimes, top floor of Foothold Citadel, the big barracks in the east of town
T 1253 | Captain Garran Vimes
A 1319 | Captain Garran Vimes
T 1284 | Captain Garran Vimes
T 1302 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 67.9, 48.2 | Clerk Lendry, on the same floor of Foothold Citadel: James Hyal
T 1252 | Captain Garran Vimes
A 1259 | Captain Garran Vimes
T 1259 | Adjutant Tesoran, in the same room
A 1285 | Adjutant Tesoran
T 1285 | Captain Garran Vimes
A 1286 | Captain Garran Vimes
T 1264 | Commander Samaul, in the same room
A 1265 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 68.0, 48.7 | Commander Samaul
T 1319 | Caz Twosprocket, the gnome at the smithy in the west of town
A 1320 | Caz Twosprocket
T 1320 | Captain Garran Vimes, back up in the citadel
C 1265 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 59.9, 40.9 | Sentry Point, the first guard tower on the road outside Theramore, just past the bridge. Walk up to it until the quest says it is explored.
T 1265 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.4, 49.3 | Archmage Tervosh, in Lady Jaina Proudmoore's tower in the middle of Theramore
A 1266 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.4, 49.3 | Archmage Tervosh

# ---------- One loop: Private Hendel and the deserters ----------
C 1204 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 61.1, 18.4 | 8 Forked Mudrock Tongues. On the way north leave the road to the east: Mudrock Spikeshells and Tortoises (36-38) walk the beach and the shallows of the north-east coast. Only about one in four has a forked tongue, so this is 30 or more kills: it is the grind of this segment, with a quest reward on top. They are slow: Frostbolt from maximum range, Frost Nova and step back, and drink between kills. Had enough? Press Skip here and on the hand-in
T 1266 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 45.2, 24.7 | Private Hendel, at the tents beside the road in the north of the marsh, west of Jarl's house. (Still owe Jarl his spices and eyes? Do his two quests now, the cavern is west of here.)
A 1324 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 45.2, 24.7 | Private Hendel
C 1324 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 45.2, 24.7 | Hendel (35) and the two guards beside him turn hostile. Fight Hendel himself: Polymorph one guard, Frost Nova Hendel and the other guard, step back, then keep casting Fireball on Hendel only (no Arcane Explosion or Cone of Cold: they wake the sheep). Mana Shield if it gets tight. He gives up when he is nearly dead. If Archmage Tervosh appears next to him afterwards, hand the quest in to him right there.
T 1286 | Balos Jacken at the Lost Point tower, south-east of the Shady Rest Inn. Take the road back west and turn south. Attack him (38): the deserters around him join in, so Polymorph one of them first, Frost Nova the rest, step back and keep casting on Jacken only. He surrenders when he is nearly dead and then talks to you. Full health and mana before you start.
A 1287 | Balos Jacken
T 1947 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 46.1, 57.1 | Mage quest. Tabetha, in her hut in the middle of the marsh: walk east from Lost Point, the hut stands just north of the Stonemaul Ruins (ogres: stay north of them). A short detour before you hearth.
A 1949 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 46.1, 57.1 | Tabetha: Hidden Secrets. Keep it: Magus Tirth is at the Mirage Raceway, where the route is again in segment 17
N Do not take Tabetha's other quest | Items of Power wants a Jade and a Bolt Charged Bramble and a return to her hut, which the route does not make. The Mage's Wand chain also needs a book from the Scarlet Monastery (a dungeon), so it stops after Magus Tirth's first quest
H Theramore | Hearthstone
T 1287 | Captain Garran Vimes. If he offers Vimes's Report (a short new quest to Lady Jaina, 290 XP), take it and hand it in at the tower in a moment.
T 1204 | Morgan Stern, in the inn. Do not take the spider follow-up: it is not on this route
T 1324 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.4, 49.3 | Archmage Tervosh in Jaina's tower (unless you already handed it in at the tents)
A 1267 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.4, 49.3 | Archmage Tervosh
T 1267 @ Dustwallow Marsh, 66.3, 49.0 | Lady Jaina Proudmoore, standing beside him
N Cast Teleport: Ironforge | Segment 15 starts there. It costs one Rune of Teleportation. No rune or no spell? Take the boat from the dock at the south-east edge of town to Menethil Harbor and fly to Ironforge. You keep for later: 1106 (Martek, Badlands), 5762 (Hemet Nesingwary, Stranglethorn), 1111 and 1178 (Ratchet), 525 (Southshore), 563 (Stormwind), 1457 and 1467 (Ironforge). Your hearthstone stays in Theramore.
